-- title:
--   Theorem 5.4 — Stop-PADM-$N_\sigma$ is $(\alpha,\varepsilon)$-RDP, exactly feasible, with expected objective gap $\tilde O(1/\sqrt n)$ and mean-square distance $\tilde O(1/n)$ to the optimum
-- statement:
--   Assume: $A$, $B$ have full row rank and $m\ge1$; $(R,P_R)$ is a probability space and $f:\mathbb R^p\times R\to\mathbb R$ is such that each $f(\cdot,d)$ is convex, differentiable and $L$-Lipschitz (Proposition 4.1), each $f(x,\cdot)$ is measurable and integrable, and $F(x)=\mathbb E_d f(x,d)$; the samplewise recovery condition $f(VAx,d)\le f(x,d)$ for all $x$ and $P_R$-a.e. $d$ (25) holds; $g$ is convex and $B$-induced $\varrho_g$-strongly convex.
--   Assume also (19) for $g$, $g(UBy)\le g(y)$ for all $y$ (for $F$ it follows from (25)). Fix $\alpha>1$, $\varepsilon>0$, $n\ge8\ln(en)$, and let $\beta$, $C$, $\sigma$ be as in Theorem 5.2. Let $u_\star$ be the fixed point of $T_F$, $y_\star=U(c-u_\star)$, and assume the conditions of Corollary 1 with $L_F=L$: for some minimizer $(\hat x_\star,\hat y_\star)$ of (16) with $u_\star=(A\hat x_\star-B\hat y_\star+c)/2$, $g$ is $L_g$-Lipschitz on the segment between $UB\hat y_\star$ and $y_\star$. Suppose that for some $M_g\ge0$
--   $$
--   g(y)-g(y_\star)\le L_g\|y-y_\star\|_2+\frac{M_g}{2}\|y-y_\star\|_2^2\qquad\forall y\in\operatorname{range}(B^\top). \tag{28}
--   $$
--   Let $\tilde u_{(0)}=A\tilde x_{(0)}$, $\tilde x_{(K)}=V\tilde u_{(K)}$, $\tilde y_{(K)}=U(c-\tilde u_{(K)})$,
--   $$
--   D_n=\frac{4\|\tilde u_{(0)}-u_\star\|_2^2}{(en)^2}+\frac{8L^2}{\varrho_g\beta\omega_A}+\frac{2m\sigma^2\beta}{\varrho_g},\qquad C_{F,g}=L\|V\|_2+L_g\|U\|_2.
--   $$
--   Then:
--
--   1. every iterate is feasible: $A\tilde x_{(k)}+B\tilde y_{(k)}=c$ for every data set, noise realisation and $k$;
--   2. Stop-PADM-$N_\sigma$ achieves $(\alpha,\varepsilon)$-RDP;
--   3. the stopped iterate $\tilde u_{(K)}$ is measurable under the joint law of data, noise and $K$;
--   4. model (1) has a unique optimal solution $(x^{\rm opt},y^{\rm opt})$ in $\operatorname{range}(A^\top)\times\operatorname{range}(B^\top)$;
--   5. for it, the objective gap is integrable and
--   $$
--   0\le\mathbb E\big[F(\tilde x_{(K)})+g(\tilde y_{(K)})-F(x^{\rm opt})-g(y^{\rm opt})\,\big|\,\Gamma_0\big]\le\frac{C_{F,g}^2}{8\beta}+C_{F,g}\sqrt{D_n}+\frac{M_g\|U\|_2^2}{2}D_n, \tag{29, 77}
--   $$
--   which is $\tilde O(1/\sqrt n)$;
--   6. the squared distance is integrable and
--   $$
--   \mathbb E\big[\|\tilde x_{(K)}-x^{\rm opt}\|_2^2+\|\tilde y_{(K)}-y^{\rm opt}\|_2^2\,\big|\,\Gamma_0\big]\le2(\|V\|_2^2+\|U\|_2^2)\Big(D_n+\frac{C_{F,g}^2}{4\beta\varrho_g}\Big), \tag{30, 79}
--   $$
--   which is $\tilde O(1/n)$.
--
--   This is the paper's headline guarantee: exact feasibility at every iteration, privacy amplification, and optimality bounds for the original constrained problem from a single pass over the data.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The expectations are over the joint law of the i.i.d. records, the i.i.d. $N(0_m,\sigma^2I_m)$ noise and $K$. $\beta$, $C$, $\sigma$, $D_n$, $C_{F,g}$ are variables bound by their defining equations. The proximal problems for every $f(\cdot,d)$ are assumed to have minimizers; those for $F$ and $g$ and the minimizers of (16) exist under the other hypotheses and are not assumed.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: Õ(1/√n) in (29) and Õ(1/n) in (30) → the explicit nonasymptotic bounds (77) with Δ_β = 0 and (79), with D_n from (73) at δ² = mσ²; reason: D_n = O(ln(en)/n) and C²_{F,g}/(8β) = O(ln(en)/n) when ‖ũ₍₀₎ − u⋆‖₂, L_g and M_g are bounded uniformly in n (the paper's uniform bounds, p.36), so the explicit bounds imply the printed rates; Õ alone has no formal content
--   - generalization: RDP and the two expectation bounds → also concludes exact feasibility of every iterate, measurability of ũ₍K₎ and integrability of the gap and the distance; reason: the proof establishes them (A.16) and they rule out junk integrals
--   - encoding: (19) for F → not stated; reason: it follows from (25) by integrating over d (F = E f); no instance changes
--   - encoding: Corollary 1's condition on the minimizer (x̂⋆, ŷ⋆) of (16) → some minimizer of (16) with u⋆ = (Ax̂⋆ − Bŷ⋆ + c)/2 and g L_g-Lipschitz on the segment [UBŷ⋆, y⋆]; the F half is implied by L_F = L; reason: Bŷ⋆ is the same for every such minimizer (Theorem 3.1 and the uniqueness of the fixed point), so the existential is the source's condition
--   - encoding: E[· | Γ₀] → plain expectation over the joint law of data, noise and K; reason: Γ₀ is generated by the deterministic ũ₍₀₎ = A x̃₍₀₎, so it is trivial
--   - encoding: u⋆ the unique fixed point of T_F → any u⋆ with T_F(u⋆) = u⋆; reason: T_F is a contraction (Proposition 5.1), so the fixed point is unique; same instances
--   - encoding: F(x) := E_{d∼P_R}[f(x, d)] → f(x, ·) measurable and P_R-integrable for every x; reason: needed for the expectation to be defined; excludes only undefined cases
--   - encoding: ω_A > 0 the smallest eigenvalue of AAᵀ → hypothesis 0 < m; reason: ω_A is undefined for m = 0
--   - encoding: sample horizon n with n ≥ 8 ln(en) → n ≥ 1 together with n ≥ 8 ln(en); reason: at n = 0 Lean's ln(0) is 0 and the window is empty; n ≥ 1 is implicit
--   - encoding: the sample proximal operators P_{β,f(·,d),A} used as everywhere defined → hypothesis that (13) for f(·,d) has a minimizer for every record d and input u; reason: Algorithm 1 is undefined otherwise; excludes only undefined cases
--   - encoding: the Rényi divergence of Definition 2 → computed through dP/dQ, +∞ when P is not absolutely continuous with respect to Q; reason: equal to Definition 2 for α > 1
--   - encoding: β, C, σ², D_n, C_{F,g} set by formulas → variables with hypotheses equating them to the formulas, σ the nonnegative square root; reason: names for the paper's values; same instances
--   - generalization: Condition 1 with C > 0 and σ > 0 (pp.9-10), that is L > 0 → L ≥ 0, including L = 0 with C = σ = 0; reason: at L = 0 the sample operators do not depend on the record and the bounds still hold; L > 0 is the source's case
--   - encoding: L_g a Lipschitz constant → hypothesis 0 ≤ L_g; reason: a Lipschitz constant is nonnegative; same instances
--   - encoding: Corollary 1's supposition that an optimal solution (x_opt, y_opt) exists → not assumed; existence and uniqueness in range(Aᵀ) × range(Bᵀ) are concluded; reason: they follow from (19) and induced strong convexity (A.16, p.35); no instance changes
-- source:
--   Li–Lai–Weng, Exact Feasibility and Privacy Amplification for Linearly Constrained Optimization, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 d58edbe0…0f3d), Theorem 5.4, p.13 (proof A.16, pp.35–36)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_padmIter
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_stopPadmLaw
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_jointLaw
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_IsRDP
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_IsOptimal
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_IsPenalizedMin
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_popLoss
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_pinvRight
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_omegaA
import Definitions.Def_LiqPremiaEq_opNorm
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_IsInducedStronglyConvex

namespace PADMPriv

open MeasureTheory

/-- Theorem 5.4 (optimality error of Stop-PADM-N_σ) of Li–Lai–Weng, *Exact Feasibility and Privacy Amplification for Linearly Constrained Optimization*, STOC 2027 submission manuscript (sha256 d58edbe0…0f3d), p.13 (proof A.16,
pp.35–36). Assume the conditions of Theorem 5.2 and Corollary 1, with `L_F = L`, together with
(19). Let `y⋆ = U(c − u⋆)` and suppose that for some `M_g ≥ 0`,
`g(y) − g(y⋆) ≤ L_g‖y − y⋆‖₂ + (M_g/2)‖y − y⋆‖₂²` for all `y ∈ range(Bᵀ)` (28). Then every iterate is
feasible, Stop-PADM-N_σ achieves `(α, ε)`-RDP, model (1) has a unique optimal solution
`(x_opt, y_opt)` in `range(Aᵀ) × range(Bᵀ)`, and with `x̃₍K₎ = Vũ₍K₎`, `ỹ₍K₎ = U(c − ũ₍K₎)`,
`D_n = 4‖ũ₍₀₎ − u⋆‖₂²/(en)² + 8L²/(ϱ_g β ω_A) + 2mσ²β/ϱ_g` and `C_{F,g} = L‖V‖₂ + L_g‖U‖₂`:
`0 ≤ E[F(x̃₍K₎) + g(ỹ₍K₎) − F(x_opt) − g(y_opt)] ≤ C_{F,g}²/(8β) + C_{F,g}√D_n + (M_g‖U‖₂²/2) D_n`
((77) with `Δ_β = 0`; this is `Õ(1/√n)`, (29)) and
`E[‖x̃₍K₎ − x_opt‖₂² + ‖ỹ₍K₎ − y_opt‖₂²] ≤ 2(‖V‖₂² + ‖U‖₂²)(D_n + C_{F,g}²/(4βϱ_g))` ((79); this is
`Õ(1/n)`, (30)).

**Formalization Note** The `Õ` rates are replaced by the explicit bounds the proof derives in A.16.
Corollary 1's condition is: some minimizer `(x̂⋆, ŷ⋆)` of (16) for `F` gives
`u⋆ = (Ax̂⋆ − Bŷ⋆ + c)/2` and `g` is `L_g`-Lipschitz on the segment between `UBŷ⋆` and `y⋆` (its `F`
half is implied by `L_F = L`); the same `L_g` appears in (28). (19) for `F` follows from (25) and is
not repeated; the proximal minimizers for `F`, `g` and the minimizers of (16) exist under these
hypotheses and are not assumed; those for every `f(·, d)` are assumed. `F(x) = E_d f(x, d)` with
`f(x, ·)` measurable and integrable. Expectations are over `jointLaw` with `N(0, σ²I_m)` noise;
`E[· | Γ₀]` is a plain expectation. `β`, `C`, `σ`, `D_n`, `C_{F,g}` are variables bound by their
defining equations. `m ≥ 1`, `n ≥ 1`. -/
theorem theorem_5_4 {m p l : ℕ} {R : Type*} [MeasurableSpace R]
    (hm : 0 < m) (A : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin p) ℝ) (B : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin l) ℝ)
    (c : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) (hA : A.rank = m) (hB : B.rank = m)
    (PR : Measure R) [IsProbabilityMeasure PR]
    (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) → R → ℝ) (L : NNReal)
    (hfconv : ∀ d, ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ (fun x => f x d))
    (hfdiff : ∀ d, Differentiable ℝ (fun x => f x d))
    (hfLip : ∀ d, LipschitzWith L (fun x => f x d))
    (hfmeas : ∀ x, Measurable (fun d => f x d)) (hfint : ∀ x, Integrable (fun d => f x d) PR)
    (hrec : ∀ x, ∀ᵐ d ∂PR,
      f (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) (Matrix.toEuclideanLin A x)) d ≤ f x d)
    (g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin l) → ℝ) (hg : ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ g) (ϱg : ℝ)
    (hgsc : IsInducedStronglyConvex B ϱg g)
    (hg19 : ∀ y, g (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (Matrix.toEuclideanLin B y)) ≤ g y)
    (α : ℝ) (hα : 1 < α) (ε : ℝ) (hε : 0 < ε) (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n)
    (hnlog : 8 * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * n) ≤ n) (β : ℝ)
    (hβdef : β = ϱg * n / (8 * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * n))) (C : ℝ)
    (hCdef : C = L / (β * Real.sqrt (omegaA A))) (σ : ℝ)
    (hσdef : σ = Real.sqrt (α * C ^ 2 *
      max (α - 1) (2 * (Real.exp 2 - 1) * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * n) / (n * ε))))
    (hfprox : ∀ d u, ∃ x, IsProxMin β (fun x => f x d) A u x)
    (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)) (ustar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m))
    (hustar : padmOp β (popLoss f PR) g A B c ustar = ustar) (Lg : ℝ) (hLg : 0 ≤ Lg)
    (hcor1 : ∃ (xh : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)) (yh : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin l)),
      IsPenalizedMin β (popLoss f PR) g A B c xh yh ∧
      ustar = (1 / 2 : ℝ) • (Matrix.toEuclideanLin A xh - Matrix.toEuclideanLin B yh + c) ∧
      ∀ y ∈ segment ℝ (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (Matrix.toEuclideanLin B yh))
          (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - ustar)),
        ∀ y' ∈ segment ℝ (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (Matrix.toEuclideanLin B yh))
            (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - ustar)),
          |g y - g y'| ≤ Lg * ‖y - y'‖)
    (Mg : ℝ) (hMg : 0 ≤ Mg)
    (h28 : ∀ y ∈ LinearMap.range (Matrix.toEuclideanLin B.transpose),
      g y - g (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - ustar)) ≤
        Lg * ‖y - Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - ustar)‖ +
          Mg / 2 * ‖y - Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - ustar)‖ ^ 2)
    (Dn : ℝ) (hDn : Dn = 4 * ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin A x₀ - ustar‖ ^ 2 / (Real.exp 1 * n) ^ 2 +
      8 * (L : ℝ) ^ 2 / (ϱg * β * omegaA A) + 2 * m * σ ^ 2 * β / ϱg)
    (CFg : ℝ) (hCFg : CFg = L * LiqPremiaEq.opNorm (pinvRight A) + Lg * LiqPremiaEq.opNorm (pinvRight B)) :
    (∀ (D : Fin n → R) (z : Fin n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) (k : ℕ),
        Matrix.toEuclideanLin A
            (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) (padmIter β f g A B c x₀ D z k)) +
          Matrix.toEuclideanLin B
            (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - padmIter β f g A B c x₀ D z k)) = c) ∧
      IsRDP α ε (fun D : Fin n → R => stopPadmLaw β σ f g A B c x₀ D) ∧
      AEMeasurable (fun ω : ((Fin n → R) × (Fin n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m))) × ℕ =>
          padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1.1 ω.1.2 ω.2) (jointLaw n PR (gaussNoise m σ)) ∧
      (∃! q : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin l),
          q.1 ∈ LinearMap.range (Matrix.toEuclideanLin A.transpose) ∧
          q.2 ∈ LinearMap.range (Matrix.toEuclideanLin B.transpose) ∧
          IsOptimal (popLoss f PR) g A B c q.1 q.2) ∧
      ∀ (xopt : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)) (yopt : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin l)),
        xopt ∈ LinearMap.range (Matrix.toEuclideanLin A.transpose) →
        yopt ∈ LinearMap.range (Matrix.toEuclideanLin B.transpose) →
        IsOptimal (popLoss f PR) g A B c xopt yopt →
        (Integrable (fun ω : ((Fin n → R) × (Fin n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m))) × ℕ =>
            let u := padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1.1 ω.1.2 ω.2
            popLoss f PR (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) u) +
              g (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - u)) - popLoss f PR xopt - g yopt)
            (jointLaw n PR (gaussNoise m σ)) ∧
          0 ≤ ∫ ω, (let u := padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1.1 ω.1.2 ω.2
              popLoss f PR (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) u) +
                g (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - u)) - popLoss f PR xopt - g yopt)
              ∂(jointLaw n PR (gaussNoise m σ)) ∧
          ∫ ω, (let u := padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1.1 ω.1.2 ω.2
              popLoss f PR (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) u) +
                g (Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - u)) - popLoss f PR xopt - g yopt)
              ∂(jointLaw n PR (gaussNoise m σ)) ≤
            CFg ^ 2 / (8 * β) + CFg * Real.sqrt Dn + Mg * LiqPremiaEq.opNorm (pinvRight B) ^ 2 / 2 * Dn) ∧
        (Integrable (fun ω : ((Fin n → R) × (Fin n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m))) × ℕ =>
            let u := padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1.1 ω.1.2 ω.2
            ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) u - xopt‖ ^ 2 +
              ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - u) - yopt‖ ^ 2)
            (jointLaw n PR (gaussNoise m σ)) ∧
          ∫ ω, (let u := padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1.1 ω.1.2 ω.2
              ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight A) u - xopt‖ ^ 2 +
                ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin (pinvRight B) (c - u) - yopt‖ ^ 2)
              ∂(jointLaw n PR (gaussNoise m σ)) ≤
            2 * (LiqPremiaEq.opNorm (pinvRight A) ^ 2 + LiqPremiaEq.opNorm (pinvRight B) ^ 2) *
              (Dn + CFg ^ 2 / (4 * β * ϱg))) := by sorry

end PADMPriv
